# Agent scratch + per-agent git worktrees. Not gitignoring this let a
# subagent's worktree (a second full checkout under .claude/worktrees/)
# land inside the lint root, so a sibling agent's `pnpm lint` reported 11
# phantom errors from the OTHER agent's copy of scripts/conductor.mjs.
.claude/

# npm pack output (release verification artifact, never committed)
*.tgz

# SAST output is a working artifact, not a record. It was committed once as a
# false clean (0 files scanned, 2 errors, exit 0) and could have been cited as
# evidence — see W21-98. Baseline it deliberately or not at all.
docs/security/semgrep-results.json
docs/security/semgrep-results.sarif
docs/security/semgrep-scan-*.log

# SAST raw output (W21-98): 1.0MB + 1.2MB, rewritten on every scan, and it
# embeds every matched source line — including the fixture credentials the
# secret rules match. docs/security/SAST_BASELINE.md and sast-baseline.json
# are the tracked record; these are the working files behind them.
docs/security/semgrep-results.json
docs/security/semgrep-results.sarif
